### Characterization and Benchmarking Methodology for Power in Networking Devices
* **Presentation:** [2. Updates to draft-ietf-bmwg-powerbench](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-bpm-updates-to-draft-ietf-bmwg-powerbench-00)
* **Presenter:** Shailesh Sathyanarayana
* **Draft:** `draft-ietf-bmwg-powerbench`
* **Details:**
  * Shailesh Sathyanarayana summarized updates made to align with feedback from the GREEN Working Group (Marisol Palmero, Benoît Claise, Chen Li).
  * Key updates include distinguishing powerbench laboratory measurement conditions from GREEN operational power states, strengthening requirements to report power meter accuracy, and explicitly scoping controlled lab benchmarking versus operational energy management.
  * Additional guidance was added for programmable data planes to require reporting installed workloads, compiler toolchains, and stateful table configurations. The authors requested a Working Group Last Call (WGLC).

