### Encrypted PDMv2 Destination Option
* **Presentation:** [3. Encrypted PDMv2](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-bpm-sessb-encrypted-pdmv2-00)
* **Presenter:** Nalini Elkins
* **Draft:** `draft-ietf-ippm-encrypted-pdmv2`
* **Details:**
  * Nalini Elkins described recent changes removing inline cryptographic negotiation (such as HPKE) to address security concerns. Security context establishment is now performed during out-of-band registration (e.g., RADIUS EAP example provided).
  * PDMv2 operates at the IP layer across upper-layer protocols (e.g., multicast QUIC video testing). An independent implementation in iPerf is planned.
  * Marcus Ihlar suggested specifying a mandatory minimum set of cryptographic algorithms for interoperability and questioned the necessity of the unencrypted option format. Nalini explained that single-party mode relies on unencrypted fields and agreed to clarify normative guidance on when unencrypted mode should or should not be used.
  * The draft needs to be renamed to reflect the BPM working group prefix.

