### Benchmarking Methodology for Source Address Validation (SAV)
* **Presentation:** [4. The Updates on the Benchmarking Methodology for Intra-domain and Inter-domain Source Address Validation](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-bpm-sessb-4-the-updates-on-the-benchmarking-methodology-for-intra-domain-and-inter-domain-source-address-validation-01)
* **Presenter:** Yipin Wang
* **Draft:** `draft-ietf-bpm-savnet-sav-benchmarking`
* **Details:**
  * Yipin Wang detailed updates aligning test scenarios and terminology with SAVNET problem statement documents (RFC 9708).
  * Refinements clarify ground truth definitions (distinguishing proper/improper blocks/permits from congestion drops), separate control-plane processing workloads from table updates and forwarding tests, and distinguish routing protocol convergence from SAV convergence.
  * Operational validation was demonstrated using the open-source SAV-OP platform in recent IETF Hackathons. Authors requested initiating WGLC. Giuseppe Fioccola advised explicitly copying the SAVNET WG on future calls for review.

