### STAMP Extensions for Reflecting MPLS Network Action Headers
* **Presentation:** [8. STAMP Extensions for Reflecting STAMP Packet MPLS Network Action Headers (draft-ietf-bpm-stamp-mpls-hdr)](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-bpm-sessb-stamp-extensions-for-reflecting-stamp-packet-mpls-network-action-headers-draft-ietf-bpm-stamp-mpls-hdr-00)
* **Presenter:** Rakesh Gandhi
* **Draft:** `draft-ietf-bpm-stamp-mpls-hdr`
* **Details:**
  * Rakesh Gandhi presented extensions allowing STAMP reflectors to copy received MPLS Network Action headers back into TLVs sent to the session sender.
  * Aligns with the companion IPv6 draft (currently in the RFC Editor queue). Requests IANA allocation for a TLV and sub-TLV. An open-source implementation (by Fabien) is available.
  * Greg Mirsky noted that because MPLS nodes pop labels and actions in transit, text should clarify the precise order of processing to ensure STAMP captures the headers before they are discarded.

