### STAMP Extensions for Residual Bit Error Rate Measurement
* **Presentation:** [9. Simple Two-Way Active Measurement Protocol (STAMP) Extensions for Residual Bit Error Rate Measurement (draft-ietf-bpm-stamp-ber-01)](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-bpm-sessb-simple-two-way-active-measurement-protocol-stamp-extensions-for-residual-bit-error-rate-measurement-draft-ietf-bpm-stamp-ber-01-00)
* **Presenter:** Rakesh Gandhi
* **Draft:** `draft-ietf-bpm-stamp-ber`
* **Details:**
  * Measures bit errors escaping FEC/CRC detection by filling STAMP extra padding with known bit patterns. The reflector checks, counts, and corrects padding errors before reflecting the packet.
  * Consolidated encoding into a single statistics TLV and an optional bit-pattern sub-TLV.
  * Discussed transport options (IPv4 vs. IPv6 UDP Lite). Commercial (Cisco) and open-source implementations exist.
  * The working group evaluated the stability of the document for IANA early allocation.

